The update of manuscript/main_text_numbers.csv for the revision of 1–2 October 2026: what was done, with the lists
from which its counts can be recounted (the table before the update is the file at the parent of the revision's text
commit).

Committed rows 1,198; rows after the update 1,381 = 1,198 − 264 deleted + 447 added.

How a committed row was carried. The committed and the revised main text were split into paragraphs (blocks between
blank lines) and the paragraphs aligned. A row of an unchanged paragraph keeps its place. In a changed paragraph the
two texts were aligned character by character; a row is carried when its number's characters are unchanged, the text
on one side of it is unchanged and the token at that place in the revised text is the row's number (a token is a whole
number as it stands in the text, its sign included). A row not carried that way is carried by one of two fallbacks,
listed below, or deleted. Every number token of the revised text without a row then received a new row, apart from the
kinds the table does not list: 95 citation years; the 13 day numbers and 11 years of the dates; 70 cross-references by
number in the running text and the captions, to the paper's own sections, tables and figures (25 after "Results", 16
after "Table" and 14 after "Fig", 10 of these before a panel letter, as in "Fig 1a") and to equations, definitions, an
example, figures and a table of cited works (7, 3, 1, 3 and 1, the last "their Table 1" of the Discussion); the 10
numbers of the captions' own heads (Fig 1 to Fig 6, Table 1 to Table 4); and the Zenodo DOI (1). A group of digits
that follows a letter directly is not a number token: the 148 in the names of the supporting items (S1 Text to S20
Table), the 4 of "Fig. S4", a figure of a cited work's appendix, and the 540 of the user name in the repository's
address. The digits of commit identifiers and the numbers inside code spans are not tokens of the text either, and the
headings are not covered: their 9 number tokens (0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7: the Results sections' numbers, "lag-0" and
"AR(1)") have no row; the title's AR(1) has one.

Rows deleted: 264. By class: 161 of the former Table 3's caption and body (the table is now the residual table of S3
Text §6); 64 of numbers the revision takes out of their paragraph (each is listed below with where it now is); 7 of
numbers that the rewritten sentences no longer state and that are at no other place in that form (each is listed below
with what became of it); 28 of labels (section numbers, dates, names, formula constants) that the rewritten sentences
no longer carry, which have no place to give; 4 of numbers that are still in their paragraph, in a rewritten sentence,
where the token has a new row with its own source.

Rows added: 447: 277 data rows (source file, line and held string), 62 design and 3 literature rows (file, line and
anchor, no held string), 19 derived rows (the derivation in place of a file) and 86 label rows (no source). Numbers
changed in place: 4 (S19 Table's count in Methods, Pre-registration and deviations: 56 to 67, 28 to 36, 14 to 15, 14
to 16).

Locators: 17 moved to the lines that the revision's edits of their source files moved them to (5 in
manuscript/supplementary.md, 1 in notes/partB5_literature_v2.md, 11 in scripts/15_figures_v2.py; 4 held strings and 5
anchors re-read on edited lines). Corrected where the audit of the revision's text found them wrong: 13 anchors of
committed rows that were not on the line they name (the values of those lines changed in B26's run); 19 committed rows
of N = 14 that named the line of column names of `results/primary_b_ts_gsr_win60.csv` (now line 48 of
`manuscript/analysis_record.md`, which gives the shape of the data), a line the 14 added rows of N = 14 take too; and
1 held string of a committed row taken from the wrong cell of its line (the Discussion's 0.003: the line's +0.0027,
not its 0.0028). One committed note reworded (1 row: the grid step of Fig 1, whose note called the surface of Fig 1a
the scope map, the plans' name). Corrected after the check of the corrected revision, all in committed rows: 13 rows
of the window sets and of the 14 subjects that named line 6 of `notes/review_results/partB/family_atoms_tables.md`, a
heading (now its line 4, which states them); 4 rows of the window sets and 1 of N = 14 in Table 2's caption that named
line 189 of the record (now the record's lines on the window sets and on the shape of the data); 5 rows of the name
AR(1), 3 of "95 %" and 1 of "lag-1" that were design rows on those lines (now label rows); the row of "BIC over 1–5"
in Methods (now line 4 of `prewhiten_tables.md`); 5 label notes that described another token of their sentence; the
note of the row on rsHRF 1.7.0, which sits on the token 1.7; the held string of 1 bound row (6.7e-16 for 5.6e-16, the
value its note names); and the notes of 2 rows that named Table 3 for values now in the residual table of S3 Text §6.
Corrected after a second check: 3 more label notes that described another token of their sentence (the 0 of "q = 0" in
Recommendations; the two 1s of "x_{t+1}, y_{t+1}" in Methods); the held string of 1 committed row, Results 2's 0.83,
which had taken the hyphen of the range "0.680-0.830" of its line for a minus sign (now 0.830, so that check_numbers
no longer flags the row); and the note of the 3 committed and 14 added rows of N = 14 that read "the per-subject rows
of the primary result", which describes neither the record's line they cite nor the result file (now "the shape of the
data: 14 subjects × 2 conditions"). After the update the anchor and the held string of every row with a line locator
are on the line it names, an anchor's prefix ("@La-b|": the row's line is one of lines a to b of its file, the rows of
a table or a single line; "@pct|": a value printed as a percentage) and the words "bound on" of a bound row's held
string being the table's notation and not text of the line.

Contexts recomputed: 281 (rows whose surrounding text the edits reached). Rows relabelled (section or paragraph): 0.
Occurrences recounted in reading order.

